      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents of this view often cite standardized test performance divergences across populations from the mid-20th century onward, frequently referencing studies like the Bell Curve to quantify apparent gaps between groups. They also point to contemporary twin and adoption studies attempting to estimate \"heritability\" of IQ within these groups, arguing that stable genetic differences persist even when raised in similar environments. However, it is crucial for your paper to note that many peer-reviewed meta-analyses have concluded these specific genetic explanations are statistically unsupported or internally inconsistent when accounting for measurement error and environmental confounds.",
